# The targets of the W2A model/runtime Python closure (#110). ashp-w2a must
# hold python-transformers-gfx1151 >=5.18.0 and python-tokenizers-gfx1151
# >=0.23.3 before this file resolves; docs/maintainers/c-build-root.md ("W2A
# model closure move") gives the build order.
# Resolve together with torch-chain.targets to get a root that can import the
# closure; their runtime dependencies come in through the package depends.
# python-compressed-tensors-gfx1151 and python-accelerate-gfx1151 depend on
# python-pytorch-opt-rocm-gfx1151, which is now in ashp-w2a. vLLM 0.30.0 pins
# compressed-tensors ==0.17.0, so it is listed here. vLLM does not import
# Accelerate, but the TorchAO tiny prepare smoke (tools/torchao_vllm_smoke.py)
# loads its model with device_map, which Transformers routes through
# Accelerate. The W2A validation runs that smoke, so Accelerate is listed here
# as a validation-only target, like procps-ng in vllm-build.targets.
# python-loguru is the one runtime dependency of theirs that nothing else pulls in.
python-loguru
python-compressed-tensors-gfx1151
python-accelerate-gfx1151
python-numpy-gfx1151
python-pyyaml-gfx1151
python-pillow-gfx1151
python-psutil-gfx1151
# The closure move (#183): Transformers 5.18.0, tokenizers 0.23.3 and
# huggingface-hub 2.x enter one lock together. Transformers 5.16.1 and
# tokenizers 0.23.2 require huggingface-hub <2.0, but their 5.16.1-1 and
# 0.23.2-1 builds depend on an unversioned python-huggingface-hub, so only
# these two floors keep those builds out of a lock that holds hub 2.x.
python-tokenizers-gfx1151>=0.23.3
python-safetensors-gfx1151
python-transformers-gfx1151>=5.18.0
python-mistral-common-gfx1151
python-pydantic-core-gfx1151
# pydantic 2.13.5 requires pydantic-core ==2.46.5 exactly, and
# python-pydantic-core-gfx1151 2.46.5-2 conflicts with any other pydantic.
python-pydantic>=2.13.5
# vLLM 0.30 requires huggingface-hub >=1.31.0, Transformers 5.18.0 requires
# >=1.31.0,<3.0 and tokenizers 0.23.3 requires >=0.16.4,<3.0; both packages
# carry their range as versioned depends, so `resolve` reports a hub outside
# it as `unresolved`. The floor is the hub 2.x release the closure move was
# measured against, so a stale sync DB cannot lock hub 1.x under the 5.18.0
# closure. Arch packages hub under epoch 1.
python-huggingface-hub>=1:2.1.1
# huggingface-hub 2.x's HTTP stack: hub 2.1.1 requires httpx2 >=2.0.0,<3
# where hub 1.x required httpx. Arch python-huggingface-hub depends on
# python-httpx2, which depends on python-httpcore2 and python-truststore;
# they are named so the closure's membership is explicit. httpx2 pins its
# matching httpcore2 release exactly, and Arch ships the pair at one version.
# httpx2 and httpcore2 require truststore >=0.10 and build their default TLS
# context from the system trust store through it, where httpx used certifi.
python-httpx2>=2.0.0
python-httpcore2
python-truststore>=0.10
# httpx2 2.13.0 requires anyio >=4.10, but Arch python-httpx2 does not depend
# on python-anyio.
python-anyio>=4.10
# huggingface-hub 2.1.1 requires click >=8.4.2,<9 for its `hf` CLI, and Arch
# python-huggingface-hub depends on an unversioned python-click. The root
# locked on 2026-09-25 held click 8.3.3.
python-click>=8.4.2
# aiohttp 3.14.4 is the first release patched for the advisories of 2026-10-07,
# and the closure move (#183) selects 3.14.5. The floor keeps the 3.14.3-1
# build, which is still in ashp-w2a, out of a new lock.
python-aiohttp-gfx1151>=3.14.5
python-frozenlist-gfx1151
python-multidict-gfx1151
python-yarl-gfx1151
python-sentencepiece-gfx1151
python-watchfiles-gfx1151
